`Bare._get_all_imports(collapse=False)` starts with `super()._get_all_imports(collapse=False)`, which for a `Bare` with no children contributes imports from vars used directly on the component. The `contents` var carries the merged `VarData`, so the superclass path already includes that merged `VarData.imports`: state-derived `$/utils/context -> StateContexts` and `react -> useContext`, plus custom `custom-lib -> Alpha, Beta as BetaAlias`, `@scope/pkg -> tag None render=False`, and extra `react -> useMemo`. Then `Bare._get_all_imports` fetches `self.contents._get_all_var_data()` and unions in `{k: list(v) for k, v in var_data.imports}`, preserving those same four keys. `VarData.merge` concatenates component tuples, so `var_data.components` contains the two embedded components in order: `Box` and `Script`.

## Answer
